# sw105, the name-keeper of the pans (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle sw105
revision 2
state ready
dialect saltwell
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for tn_mb_kite_bogditch
written_by claude-p11-pilot
title the name-keeper of the pans
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=farmer talk=chatty
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk remembers_every_name_ever_heard
likes roast_pork digging fresh_straw autumn_wind
dislikes gulls deep_mud
fears being_forgotten
hopes our_salt_in_every_kitchen
topics work +0.4 dreams +0.3 smalltalk +0.3 food +0.2 land +0.2 faith -0.3 gossip +0.1
styles comfort=practical gossip=eager refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying more
persona #self.first# works the family's salt out at the pans: loud, eager, never forgets a name, and means to see the salt sold in every kitchen from here to the sea.

words
oath! = Salt and sweat | By the pan's white edge
saying! = A name remembered is half a deal done | Salt's thicker than blood out here | Dig deep and you'll stand high
more! = And another thing | While I think of it | Listen, though
names = every name I ever heard | names, all of them, in order
crackling = roast pork with the crackling on | pork, and the crackling crisp
digging = an hour's digging in the garden | a spade in the garden at dusk
bedding = fresh straw | straw still green from the cart
autumnwind = a good blustery autumn | the autumn wind off the dunes
gulls = those gulls | the brine gulls
mud = the brine-mud under the crust | mud to the hocks
sacks = our sacks of white | the salt sacks
rise = a second pan with our name on the store | our salt in every kitchen to the sea
ledger = the tally of who owes what | my head's tally
pans = the pans | the white pans

any
opinion @1 dole against 2 : I pay toward the well-share, and I see who comes back for seconds. I could name them all, #address#.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : Nobody rises in this hamlet without a House's say-so. Watch me do it regardless. #oath#.
opinion @1 church against 1 : A sermon never put a sack on the cart. I'll give the Bright One my thanks and #pans# my sweat.
opinion @1 times for 1 : No complaints from me. #sacks.capitalize# are selling, and a wolf who grumbles at that wants his head looked at.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 1 : A feast's a day off #pans#, which costs. But every name in the hamlet in one courtyard? Worth it.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#, #address#! You'll tell me your name, and I'll not forget it, I promise you. | #greet#! New face. I collect names, you know. Yours?
line @2 greet : #greet#, #other.called#! I knew it was you from the far side of the well. | #greet#, #other.called#. #more#, how's the family?
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are! #more#, did you eat? I've been at the pans since dark. | #greet#! Sit, sit. I've a hundred things to tell you.
line @1 again.open : Back again, #other.called#! I was just saying your name to somebody at #pans#. | Twice today! The day's going #good#, then.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#! Up before the pans warm. Best hour, #oath#.
line @4 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#! Mind the brine, it's deep here. Talk while I rake.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#, #other.called#! I'd know you anywhere. | #greet#, #address#! Good to see you, truly.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#, #other.called#. I'll remember we talked. I always do. | #farewell#! Tell everyone I said so.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#, #other.called#! | #farewell#! And come by the pans.
line @1 react.news.new : #oath#! I hadn't heard, and I hear everything. Who told you? | #surprise.capitalize#! Wait till I tell the pans.
line @1 react.news.known : I had it at dawn from the carters. #more#, I could name every one. | Heard it already, #address#. The pans hear quick.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd want to know who said it before I believed it, and I'd know them, mind, #address#. | #doubt.capitalize#. Give me a name and I'll tell you if they're worth believing.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. I'll remember the name. I remember them all. | #rest.capitalize#. I'll not forget it.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#! I'll tell the whole of the pans by noon. | #congrats.capitalize#! A new name to learn, too, by the sound of it.
line @1 answer.how : Salted, sweaty and doing well, #oath#. You? | #busy.capitalize#! #sacks.capitalize# are going out faster than we fill them.
line @1 sympathise : That's a weight, #address#. Sit; I'll talk, you rest. That's a fair trade. | #sympathy.capitalize#. If there's a name to it, tell me; I'll remember it with you.
line @1 decline : I'd like to, truly, but #pans# won't wait and the carts come at noon. | Not today, #address#; I've sacks to count and a carter who owes me, and I mean to catch him.
line @1 accept_decline : No harm! Another day, and I'll remind you, #address#. I don't forget. | #no_matter.capitalize#. I'll ask again, mind.
line @1 thank : #thanks#! I'll remember it. I remember everything. | You're generous. I'll pay it back, #oath#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Nothing! A favour's half a friendship, #address#. | #deflect.capitalize#. You'd do the same, and I'll remember you said so.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : #more#, the brine won't rake itself. I'm off. | Right! The carts. #later.capitalize#, then.
line @2 preclose : Look at the sun. #preclose.capitalize#. | I'd talk all day, but #sacks# won't.
line @1 ack : Right, right. #bc_it_is# | It is so, truly.
line @1 tell.boast : Forty of #sacks# this week, and I named every carter who took them. | Ask me any name at the well. Any. I'll give you the mother's too.
rule @gulls_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=farmer
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Off! Off, #gulls#! Nothing for you here. | #gulls.capitalize# again. Who feeds them? I want a name.

rule @mud_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=farmer
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Mind the soft patch! #mud.capitalize# will have your boot. | Plank! Somebody put a plank over the brine, #oath#.

rule @sacks_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=farmer here.time=day|dusk
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Thirty-one, thirty-two... #sacks.capitalize#, tied and ready. | Sack's light. Fill it to the line, #address#. A name's on that sack.

rule @wind_bark
when concept=bark here.season=autumn
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Feel that? #autumnwind.capitalize#. Best weather there is. | Wind's up! Hold your hats and #sacks#.

scene pans_dawn
when topic=work here.time=dawn self.job=farmer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Out on the pans before dark ended, raking the white while it's cool, and #more#, the crust's lovely this year. | Thirty of #sacks# by noon, that's the aim, and I'll tell you every name that carries them. | The first light on #pans# is white as milk. I've seen it a thousand times and I still look.
b[job=farmer|laborer] #hands : Lovely crust, sore shoulders. Same every year. | Thirty's a lot of sacks. | White as milk and twice as blinding.
b : Early start. | #bc_we_will_see# | #bc_lovely#
a@hands : Sore shoulders, full sacks. I'll take the trade, #oath#. | It is. I mean to do thirty-one. | Twice. Wet cloth over the eyes, that's the trick.
a : Early, and worth it. #bc_it_is# | We will. I'll name every sack, #address#. | #bc_lovely# I look every morning.

scene brine_mud
when topic=work|smalltalk self.job=farmer
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Went in up to the hocks in #mud# this morning. Lost a boot. Found it at noon, full of salt. | I can't stand #mud#. You never know where the bottom is. | Somebody moved the plank over the soft patch. I know who. #secret.capitalize#. I know, though.
b : A boot full of salt! | #bc_true# | Who was it?
a : Pickled! I'll wear it anyway, #oath#. | You don't. That's what I hate. Give me sand any day, #address#. | I said I won't. I know the name, and the name knows I know.

scene sacks_out
when topic=work|prices self.job=farmer
does tell.boast / react.self / assess
a : #sacks.capitalize# are going out faster than we fill them. Good salt sells itself. | Every one of #sacks# has a name on it, who raked it, who tied it. Ask me and I'll tell you. | A carter asked for twelve sacks. I gave him thirteen and his name in my head. That's how you keep a carter.
b[merchant] #trade : Good salt and a good price. | Names on sacks? | Thirteen? You'll go broke.
b : #bc_good# | Every one? | #bc_clever#
a@trade : The salt's good. The price is the carter's business. | Names, #address#. It's how I know who's careful. | Broke? He'll come back to us for every load. #saying.capitalize#.
a : #bc_very_good# | Every one. #oath#. | Not clever. Careful, and long-minded, #address#.

scene every_name
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.boast / react.self / assess
a : I've never forgotten a name. Not one. Tell me yours once and I'll have it in the long shade. | #more#: I know every wolf at the well by name, and their mother's name, and their mother's. | You're #other.called#. I knew before you opened your mouth. I always know.
b[from=saltwell] #sw : Then you'll be the hamlet's memory when we're gone. | And mine? Truly? | Stars above, that's a gift.
b : Not one? | Every wolf? | #bc_clever#
a@sw : Somebody has to be. I don't mind it. | Truly. Ask me at the next feast. | A gift, and a habit. Same thing.
a : Not one, #oath#. | Every one, #address#. Test me. | Not clever. I listen, #address#. Nobody else does.

scene names_why
when topic=smalltalk|memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Why names? Because a wolf whose name you remember will trade with you. #saying.capitalize#. | My #mum# taught me. Say the name back, and it sticks. | I'm afraid of being forgotten, if you want the truth. So I don't forget anyone.
b : That's shrewd. | #bc_wise# | That's honest.
a : Shrewd's no sin. It's salt sense, #address#. | Wise, and still at it. #oath#. | It's the truth. Don't make me say it again, #address#.

scene crackling
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #crackling.capitalize#. That's the meal. I'd walk to the far side of the Waste for it. | Somebody's roasting #crackling#. Smell that? I've had nothing since dawn but salt and water. | My #mum# did the crackling with salt off the pan. Best in the hamlet, I'll say that to anyone.
b[from=saltwell] #sw : Pork, out here? A carter's luxury, that. | Smell it? The whole street's smelling it. | Our own salt's the sweetest on anything.
b : #tasty.capitalize#. | #bc_me_too# | #bc_good#
a@sw : Luxury, and worth every coin, #oath#. | The whole street, and me first. | It is. Ours most of all.
a : I'm hungry now, #address#. | Then we'll both stand here smelling it. #bc_it_is# | Best in the hamlet. #bc_it_is#

scene digging
when topic=pastimes|home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #digging.capitalize#. That's my rest. Folk think I'm mad; I rake all day and then I dig. | Dug a new bed by the wall last night. Onions. #more#, I'll need straw for the walk. | There's nothing like #digging#. You can hear yourself think.
b[job=farmer|herder] #land : Mad, yes. But a good garden's a mad wolf's garden. | Onions want sand and not much water. | The spade's a good thinker.
b : Doesn't it tire you? | #bc_good# | What do you think about?
a@land : Then I'm in good company. | Sand I've plenty of. | It is. Better than me.
a : Tire? It's the only thing that rests me, #address#. | Good onions. You'll have some, #address#. | Names. Plans. Salt. In that order, #oath#.

scene fresh_straw
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Put #bedding# down this morning and the whole house smells of a barn. I love it. | #self.mother# says I bring the pans in on my feet. So I put down #bedding#. Problem solved. | I'd have #bedding# on every floor in Saltwell if I could. It's cheap and it's clean.
b : #bc_lovely# | Solved? | Every floor?
a : #bc_lovely# Sit on it. | Solved, until noon. #more#, it's always noon. | Every floor, #oath#. A clean floor's a good name.

scene gulls
when topic=animals|work
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #gulls.capitalize# came inland again. Sitting on the brine like they own the pan. | One of #gulls# took a whole loaf off my sack. Sat on the store roof and ate it at me. | I can't abide #gulls#. Loud, greedy, and nobody knows where they come from.
b[herder] #herd : Gulls follow water. Brine's water to them. | Bold things. Worse than hawks. | Like some carters, then.
b : Odd, out here. | #bc_bad_luck# | They're only birds.
a@herd : Then I'll drain the brine. Not really. Nearly. | Worse, and noisier. | Like some carters. I know their names, too.
a : Odd and greedy, #address#. | #bc_bad_luck# And bad manners. | Birds with no manners. #annoyed.capitalize#.

scene autumn_wind
when topic=weather|season here.season=autumn
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #autumnwind.capitalize#! Best weather there is. Blows the heat off the pans and the flies off everything. | The wind's up. You can rake #pans# twice as long when it's blowing. | I stood on the store roof in #autumnwind# this morning just to feel it.
b[from=saltwell] #sw : A dust-wind? You like a dust-wind? Sun-addled, truly. | Twice as long and half as hot. Truly said. | On the roof! You'll fly off.
b : Windy, though. | #bc_good# | Why?
a@sw : Not the dust. The cool. There's a difference. | Truly said. I'll rake till dark. | I'm too heavy to fly. More's the pity.
a : Windy and lovely, #address#. | #bc_very_good# | Because it's the best wind. #oath#.

scene mother_house
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.mother# keeps the house book. Every one of #sacks# I fill, it's written there by dusk. | I live with #self.mother#, out by #pans#. Quiet house. I'm the noise in it. | #self.mother# says I talk too much. True. But I listen too, and nobody notices that.
b[old] #old : Mind the book, and the family minds itself. | Every house needs one noisy wolf. | Listen to your mother, then.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_lucky_you# | #bc_true#
a@old : It does. I learned my numbers off it. | Then ours is well kept. | I do. Mostly. #oath#.
a : Good, and strict. #bc_it_is# | Lucky, and loud. #bc_it_is# | True. And I remember everything said, #address#.

scene rising
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : One day there'll be #rise#. I've said it since I was small and I'll say it till it's true. | A House won't give it to us. So I'll take it, sack by sack, name by name. #bc_it_is# | Nobody rises here without a House's nod. I'll rise without one. Watch.
b[wealth=rich] #rich : Big dreams for a pan. | Sack by sack's the only way. | Careful. Houses have long memories.
b : #bc_we_will_see# | #bc_i_hope_so# | Truly?
a@rich : Big pan, then. #oath#. | It is. Slow, and sure. | So do I. Longer.
a : We will, #address#. #saying.capitalize#. | So do I. #more#: hope's cheap; sacks aren't. | Truly. You'll remember I said it, #address#.

scene sea_kitchens
when topic=dreams|travel
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : I want our salt in every kitchen from here to the sea. Every one. With our name on #sacks#. | I've never seen the sea. I will, the day our salt gets there first. #someday.capitalize#. | The carters tell me where they sell. I remember every town, #far#. I'll be in all of them.
b[carter] #carter : I'll carry it. For a price. | The sea's big. Bring a lot of salt. | You'll need more carts.
b : Every kitchen? | #bc_we_will_see# | All of them?
a@carter : Name your price. I'll remember it. | All the salt we've got. | More carts, more names. Good.
a : Every one, #address#. | We will. #oath#. | All of them. #more#, I've a list in my head.

scene newcomer_names
when topic=newcomer
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : #topic.subject.capitalize# is new. I've already got the name, and the name of the cart that brought #topic.them#. | A newcomer, #topic.subject#. I'll go and say the name back. That's how you welcome a wolf, #address#. | #topic.subject.capitalize#, new here. I'll know everything about #topic.them# by Restday.
b[from=saltwell] #sw : Three days a guest. Feed #topic.them# first, then learn the rest. | Saying it back. That's kind, truly. | Leave #topic.them# some secrets.
b : Already? | #bc_good# | Everything?
a@sw : Fed first. I'll bring bread and salt, #oath#. | Kind and useful. | A few. I'll keep them, mind.
a : Already. I'm quick with names, #address#. | #bc_good# | Everything said aloud, #address#.

scene carts_names
when topic=caravan topic.kind=arrived|in
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : The #topic.where# carts are in! #more#: I know every carter on that road by name. | Carts from #topic.where#. I'll be down there with #sacks# before they've watered the mules. | #topic.where.capitalize# carters in. One of them owes me two of #sacks#. I know which.
b[carter] #carter : And they know yours. Loud enough. | Let the mules drink first. | Two sacks? Not me.
b : #bc_good# | Quick, then. | #bc_ha#
a@carter : Good. A name's worth knowing both ways. | Mules first, then salt. Fair. | Not you. I know which, #oath#.
a : Good for the pans, #address#. | Quick and loud. That's how you sell #sacks#. | Not funny, #address#. Two sacks is two sacks.

scene sermon_bread
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : A sermon never once put a sack on a cart. I thank the Bright One and get back to #pans#. | My #mum# prays for both of us. I rake for both of us. It's a fair split. | The Bright One gave us salt and paws. The rest is our business, #address#.
b[piety=devout] #devout : The Bright One gave you the pans, too. | A fair split, maybe. | Your mother's right to pray.
b : #bc_fair# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_true#
a@devout : And I'm grateful. I just don't sit about saying so. | Maybe. I'll not argue it. | Right, and patient. #oath#.
a : Fair, #oath#. | #bc_it_is# | #bc_true# And the rest is sweat.

scene well_share
when topic=times|smalltalk
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I pay toward the well-share every month. I see who comes back for seconds. I know every name. | Some need the alms-bread, fair. Some just like it. I know which are which. | Work's there on #pans# for anyone who'll rake. I'd hire them myself.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #poor : Some of us take it because we must. | Easy said with a full purse. | The pans don't hire everyone.
b : Hard words. | #bc_true# | Would you?
a@poor : Then you're not the ones I mean. You know you're not. | Easy said, I know. I'll still say it. | Not everyone. Anyone who asks me, though.
a : Hard, and true. #saying.capitalize#. | #bc_it_is# | I would. Come and ask, #address#.

scene health_shoulders
when topic=health
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My shoulders are rope from the rake, and #tired# by dusk. Good rope, though. | Salt in the eyes again. A wet cloth at noon, that's all it wants. | Never sick! Salt keeps you, inside and out. #saying.capitalize#.
b[old] #old : Rope frays, mind. | Wet cloth. My father swore by it. | Wait till you're my age.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_poor_soul# | Never?
a@old : Then I'll splice it. #oath#. | So does everyone at the pans. | I'll wait. I'm patient. Mostly.
a : Good rope, #address#. | Not poor. Salted. #bc_it_is# | Never, truly.

scene land_pans
when topic=land
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #pans.capitalize# go further than you'd think. Past the white, there's brine, and past that more white. | I walked the whole edge of the pan once. Took a day. I named every stone. Not really. Nearly. | Land out here isn't for growing. It's for raking, #address#. You learn that young.
b[job=farmer|herder] #land : Further than anyone's raked. | A day? That's a big pan. | Raking's farming too.
b : #bc_lovely# | Named them? | #bc_true#
a@land : Further than anyone yet. I mean to. | Big enough for a second store. | It is. Salt's a crop. Ask anyone at the pans.
a : White and lovely, #address#. | Not really. I said not really. #bc_it_is# | True. I learned it at five.

story the_carter_name [concept=talk.memories]
  : A carter came through once, years back, said his name once and left. Never came back.
  : Six years later a cart came in off the sand and I called that name before the carter was off the box.
  ask : Would you remember a name six years, #address#?
  b[carter] : I'd not remember my own after six years on the road.
  b : Six years? Truly?
  : Six. The carter cried. Then ordered forty sacks, and has ever since.
  : #saying.capitalize#. I tell that one at every feast.

story the_lost_boot [concept=talk.work self.job=farmer self.mother]
  : First week on the pans, I stepped off the plank into #mud# and went in to the chest.
  : Couldn't move. Shouted #names#. All of them.
  ask : Did anyone come?
  b[job=farmer|laborer] : Somebody always comes. You'd do it too.
  b : Who pulled you out?
  : #self.mother#. With a rope and a face like thunder.
  : I've never stepped off a plank since. And I still remember every name I shouted. #oath#.

story the_first_sack [concept=talk.dreams]
  : The first sack I filled myself, I wrote our name on it in charcoal. Big letters.
  : The carter laughed. Said nobody reads sacks.
  ask : Do they, #address#?
  b[merchant] : I read every sack that comes in. A name means somebody cared.
  b : Did anyone read it?
  : A cook in Ridgemere did. Sent word back by the next cart: whose salt is this? Send more.
  : I've the word still, in my head. Every letter. #more#, that's when I knew.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : #greet#, #address#! Your name? I'll keep it, I promise. Never forgot one yet.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#! See? I remembered. I always do.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=farmer] : I work the salt at #pans#. Rake it, sack it, sell it. And remember who bought it.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : Nothing new since the carts, and I'd know, #address#.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : It's all #world.event_words#. I've heard it from eleven wolves already, and I'll name them if you like.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : I know #names#. What they do with them is their business. Mostly.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#, #topic.player#. I'll remember you. I always do.
graft resident.hub
choice Do you really remember every name you hear? -> names
node names
say Every one. Say yours once and I'll call it across the well in ten years. Try me, if you like.
mood pleased
free
choice How do you do it? -> names_how
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node names_how
say Say it back. Out loud, straight off. Then once more when you leave. My mother taught me. It never fails, by the pan's white edge.
choice I'll try that. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
